# The API base URL is NOT set here. It is a build-time fact (it ships inside the
# public bundle), so it lives in committed, mode-specific files that Vite selects
# automatically — nothing to edit per build:
#
#   .env.development  → used by `vite` / `npm run dev`   (http://localhost:3000/api/v1)
#   .env.production   → used by `vite build`             (https://api.cortexapp.me/api/v1)
#
# To override a value for YOUR machine, create a mode-specific local file
# (gitignored) — it outranks the committed mode file. For dev that is
# .env.development.local; a plain .env.local does NOT win over .env.development.
# e.g. to point local dev at a tunnel, in web/.env.development.local:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-tunnel-host.example.com/api/v1
